From 487a6a02c7e657d97f488983f527ad30c6feb9e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luannt <luannt.devops@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:51:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): coordinator readiness wait no longer races
 concurrent agent builds

The coordinator kept one errgroup for "agents are built" and called Go on it
from buildAgent while turns called Wait. buildAgent runs on every turn (through
the agent tool) and on every UpdateAgent, so with several concurrent runs a Go
from zero raced a Wait and the server panicked with "sync: WaitGroup is reused
before previous Wait has returned", killing every client of the project
(27/200 trials with 10 concurrent runs before, 0/280 after).

readyGroup replaces the errgroup with a mutex, a pending counter and a per
generation idle channel. Go/Wait keep their signatures and semantics: a turn
waits until every build, nested ones included, has finished, and the first
error sticks as before. TestRunWaitIsSafeAgainstConcurrentAgentBuild drives the
bad order and fails with DATA RACE on the old code under -race.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
